{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And from the lands</b> — He mentioned east and west, for thus the inhabited world extends from one end to the other." "<b>And he mentioned north</b> — for there is the entirety of civilization, and he did not mention south because of the sun's heat; there is no settlement there in complete proofs." "<b>And the meaning of \"and waters\"</b> — those who go down to the sea, for \"those who go down\" is written among the four mentioned, and so he mentions those who go down to the sea and afterward it is written: \"Let them give thanks to YHWH for His kindness.\" And some say: action." "<b>\"Let the redeemed of YHWH say\"</b> — He it is who redeemed them from the hand of the enemy." "<b>And let them give thanks to YHWH</b> — the words of the poet to the four mentioned."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 107, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:54.368219187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}